<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Aquarium World – Accessibility</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/style.css">
  <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="16x16" href="/favicon/favicon-16x16.png">
</head>

<body>

<div class="bubbles">
  <span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span>
  <span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span>
</div>

<header>
  <%- include('partials/header', { subtitulo: 'Accessibility' }) %>
</header>

<div class="opening-times">
  <strong>Opening Times:</strong> Open every day from 9:00am to 6:00pm.
  <span id="live-time" class="live-time"></span>
</div>

<div class="everything">
  <h1>Accessibility at Aquarium World</h1>
  <p>We're committed to making your visit enjoyable for everyone.</p>
</div>

<section id="about">
  <div class="info-box">
    <h2>Our Commitment</h2>
    <p>At Aquarium World, everyone is welcome. We strive to provide an inclusive environment for guests with visible and non-visible disabilities, including autism, sensory sensitivities, mobility impairments, hearing and vision loss, and other accessibility needs. Our facilities are fully wheelchair accessible, assistance animals are welcome, and our friendly team is always available to offer support so every visitor can enjoy an unforgettable experience.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="everything">
  <h3>Accessibility Details</h3>
</div>

<div class="acessibilidade-flex">
  <img src="/res/imagens/wheelchairgirl.png" alt="Menina em cadeira de rodas acenando">

 <section class="zone-drawers">
    <div class="firstblock">

      <details class="drawer" open>
        <summary>Mobility</summary>
        <p>Every route through the aquarium is step-free, with ramps and lifts connecting all levels. Wheelchairs and mobility scooters can be borrowed free of charge at the entrance, and accessible parking bays are available close to the main doors.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="drawer" open>
        <summary>Visual</summary>
        <p>Guests who are blind or have low vision can take part in guided touch experiences at the Touch Pool with a staff member close by. Signage throughout the aquarium uses high-contrast lettering, and large-print guides are available at the front desk on request.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="drawer" open>
        <summary>Autism &amp; Neurodivergent Guests</summary>
        <p>Quieter viewing sessions with dimmed lighting and lower sound levels are held before opening hours for guests who find busy spaces overwhelming. A visual story showing what to expect on a visit is available in advance, and a quiet room is on hand if anyone needs a break during the day.</p>
      </details>

    </div>

    <div class="Secondblock">

      <details class="drawer" open>
        <summary>Hearing</summary>
        <p>All exhibit videos are captioned, and written transcripts of keeper talks are available at the information desk. Staff trained in basic British Sign Language are on site during peak hours, and induction loops are fitted at the main reception.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="drawer" open>
        <summary>Assistance Animals</summary>
        <p>Registered assistance animals are welcome throughout every zone of the aquarium, including areas where pets aren't normally permitted. Water bowls are available near the entrance, and staff can point out the most comfortable route for you and your animal.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="drawer" open>
        <summary>Website Accessibility</summary>
        <p>This website is built with accessibility in mind: pages use clear heading structures so screen readers can navigate them easily, every image includes descriptive alt text, and all interactive elements can be reached and used with a keyboard alone. Text and background colours are chosen to keep good contrast throughout.</p>
      </details>

    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<div class="acessibilidade-flex2">
  <img src="/res/imagens/groupaccessibility.png" alt="Group of people with different accessibility needs, including a person in a wheelchair, a person with a cane, and a person with a hearing aid">
</div>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>

<script src="/scripts/main.js"></script>

</body>
</html>